Done. The fix:

**`lib/reply.js:1001`** — the `'finish'` listener fires with no argument, so `err` was `undefined` at the call site, contradicting the `Error | null` contract in `types/logger.d.ts` and the JSDoc in `lib/log-controller.js`:

```js
function onResponseCallback (err, request, reply) {
  // `err` is `undefined` when the response finished without errors, but the
  // LogController contract states it receives `Error | null`.
  reply.server[kLogController].requestCompleted(err ?? null, request, reply)
}
```

I normalized at runtime rather than widening the typings, since the declared `Error | null` matches the documented contract and the existing internal tests (`test/internals/logger.test.js:223` already calls it with `null`).

**`test/logger/logging.test.js`** — added a case that subclasses `LogController` and asserts `requestCompleted` receives exactly `null` for a successful request (plan bumped 16 → 17).

`node --test test/logger/logging.test.js`: 18/18 pass. Nothing committed.

